# Trellis: the spec layer is tracked (durable, reviewable contracts); task
# state, journals, runtime and scripts stay local. Three lines, in this order,
# and none of them is redundant:
#   !.trellis/       re-includes the directory itself. Without it the
#                    machine-wide core.excludesFile rule `.trellis/` still hides
#                    the whole tree, git never descends, and the negation below
#                    is dead. Verify with `git check-ignore -v`, not by eye.
#   .trellis/*       ignores the direct children. A negation under a fully
#                    ignored parent cannot work, so this must be `*`.
#   !.trellis/spec/  re-includes the one subtree we track.
!.trellis/
.trellis/*
!.trellis/spec/
audit-report-favbase-2026-07-08.html
audit-report-favbase-2026-07-08.md
.impeccable/
output/
